3. Touch the dry toothpick tip to the rhinestone to pick it up, then press onto the wet top coat dot.
4. Once set, seal the entire nail with top coat (go around the gem, not directly over it, to keep it raised).

*Pro tip: Let the top coat anchoring dot get slightly tacky before placing the gem  20 seconds. It grips better than fully wet.*

