A curved piece of tape placed at the cuticle end creates a clean arc that separates two colours. This is one of the most-searched simple nail designs for beginners because the result looks like salon work.

**Tool substitute:** Scotch tape curved and pressed lightly at the cuticle.

1. Paint entire nail in base colour. Dry completely (minimum 10 minutes  this matters).
2. Cut a small piece of tape and curve it over the lower half of the nail, covering the cuticle area.
3. Paint the exposed tip portion in your second colour.
4. Peel tape immediately while the second colour is still wet. Seal with top coat.

*Pro tip: Press the tape firmly at the curved edge but lightly everywhere else. A firm edge = a clean line.*

