One diagonal piece of tape divides the nail into two colour zones. One of the best nail art with tape designs for beginners because the asymmetry means imperfect placement still reads well.

**Tool substitute:** Scotch tape placed diagonally across the nail.

1. Paint entire nail in first colour. Dry completely.
2. Place tape diagonally from one lower corner to the opposite upper corner.
3. Paint the exposed triangle in your second colour.
4. Remove tape while wet. Top coat once dry.

*Pro tip: Go from light to dark  paint the lighter colour as the base and the darker colour as the triangle. It gives better contrast even if the line isn't perfectly straight.*

