Two colours blending from one side of the nail to the other. One of the best <strong>easy nail designs for beginners</strong> for shaky hands because the blending hides any unevenness.

**Tool substitute:** Corner of a makeup sponge or a kitchen sponge.

1. Apply a light base colour and dry.
2. Paint two colours side by side on the sponge edge, overlapping slightly in the centre.
3. Dab the sponge onto the nail with light, quick presses. Build colour with more presses.
4. Clean edges with a cotton swab in acetone. Seal with top coat.

*Pro tip: Three to five dabs builds the colour gradually. Too many dabs in one spot makes it patchy rather than blended.*

