## How to Fix a Nail Art Mistake Without Starting Over

You don't need to start over. Here is what to do in the next 30 seconds.

**If the polish is still wet:** Dip a cotton swab in acetone and press it lightly against the mistake. Acetone dissolves wet polish immediately. Clean the edge and let it dry before touching it again. Do not rub  press, then lift.

**If the polish is already dry:** Use a toothpick to gently scrape away the dried edge. This works better than you'd expect on fully cured polish. Scrape toward the edge of the mistake, not across it. Then touch up with your base colour using the very tip of the brush, let dry, and seal again with top coat.

**If the whole nail is smudged:** Paint over it. Apply one thin coat of your base colour directly over the smudge. This re-levels the surface. Let it dry, then re-apply the design.

The single most common mistake is touching the nail too soon. Most regular polishes feel dry to the touch in 5 minutes but are actually still soft underneath for another 10 to 20 minutes. If you smudge a nail you thought was dry, that's why. Wait longer than you think you need to.

Acetone-based nail polish remover on a small cotton swab is your primary repair tool. Keep it next to you during every design session, not in the bathroom cabinet.

