## Your First Design: Where to Actually Start

Start with Design 1. Polka Dot Nails.

**What is the easiest nail art design to do at home?** Polka dots with a toothpick. Two polishes you already own. No lines, no precision, no timing pressure. Every dot looks right regardless of size or spacing. It's the design that builds the evidence that you can do this  which is the only prerequisite for every design after it.

After polka dots, the natural second design depends on what you want to try. For tape, go to Design 8 (Diagonal Colour Block)  the easiest tape introduction. For sponge, go to Design 14 (Glitter Gradient Tips)  the most forgiving sponge technique. For a 2026 trend, Design 20 (Milky Glazed Nails) requires no art at all, just layering and chrome powder.

Pick one design for tonight. Do it on one accent nail if you want, not all ten. One successful nail is more useful than ten attempted ones. Your confidence with the technique grows from finishing something, not from ambition on the first try.

Regular polish works for every design here. Gel gives you more working time between coats, but it requires a UV lamp and more equipment. Start with what you already have. The jump to gel, if you want to make it, comes after you know which designs you actually enjoy.

